# Line endings and binary handling.
#
# This replaces an auto-generated file that sent every binary type to Git LFS.
# LFS was dropped deliberately: the largest asset actually tracked here is a
# 221 KB JPEG, which is three orders of magnitude below GitHub's 100 MB
# per-file limit, and LFS would have cost every clone a separate download
# against a 1 GB/month free bandwidth allowance. See .gitignore for where the
# genuinely large binaries went instead.

# Store text as LF in the repository, check out with the platform default.
* text=auto

# The Figma Make helpers are extension-less bash scripts, so the `* text=auto`
# rule above cannot tell them apart from binaries by content alone on every
# platform. Pinned to LF explicitly: a CRLF after the shebang makes
# `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` an interpreter that does not exist, and the script
# dies with "bad interpreter" on Linux and macOS.
.figma/make/analyze-routes text eol=lf
.figma/make/deploy         text eol=lf
.figma/make/deploy-preview text eol=lf
.figma/make/dev            text eol=lf
.figma/make/format         text eol=lf
.figma/make/install        text eol=lf
.figma/make/langserver     text eol=lf

# Source and config. eol=lf rather than the platform default so a file edited
# on Windows and then on macOS does not show up as wholly rewritten, and so
# oxfmt has one consistent input.
*.ts    text eol=lf
*.tsx   text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.sql   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf

# Binary. Marked so Git never attempts newline conversion on them — a single
# rewritten byte destroys an image or a PDF — and so diffs stay out of them.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary

# The lockfile has to round-trip byte-for-byte. If Git normalises it, pnpm can
# decide the lockfile no longer matches package.json and resolve the whole
# dependency tree again, which is how a reproducible build stops being one.
pnpm-lock.yaml -text
